  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 251 AM CDT Sat Oct 10 2026\n\nModel guidance continues to be in good agreement on Monday with\nridging remaining across the Midwest and a front remaining to \nthe north of the CWA. This will set up southwesterly flow across\nthe CWA at the same time 850mb temperatures will be around 20C \nwhich is the 99th percentile for this time of year. Temperatures\nwill be near or at record warmth (see climate section) \nincluding the monthly record of 94 degrees at St. Louis. The \nwarmth will continue into Tuesday, but available guidance \ncontinues to indicate a front will move south into the area \nduring the day resulting in a large variability in highs north \nof I-70.\n\nShowers will become likely with a chance for thunderstorms starting \nTuesday night that continues through Thursday as the LREF is showing \nthe upper ridge breaking down and the aforementioned front becoming \nquasi-stationary across Missouri and Illinois.  It is during this \nperiod when 40-60% of the LREF members are producing rain at St. \nLouis. The cluster analysis is showing an increasing spread with how \ndeep a trough will be over the Great Lakes which ultimately will \ndetermine how quickly we dry out and cool off by next weekend.  At \nthis point it looks like we will see highs in the 70s and 80s on \nWednesday and Thursday behind the front on Tuesday with the \npotential for cooler weather by next weekend.",
